  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <exercise id="_4b80f75e-83fa-47fa-908b-5f41956b3084" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">Use the following to answer questions 1 – 7.</para>
          <para id="para-00003">The table shows values of the expressions <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <table class="os-raise-skinnytable" id="table-00001">
            <tgroup cols="3">
              <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis></entry>
                  <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis></entry>
                  <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis></entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>\(1\)</entry>
                  <entry>\(10\)</entry>
                  <entry>\(2\)</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>\(2\)</entry>
                  <entry>\(40\)</entry>
                  <entry>\(4\)</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>\(3\)</entry>
                  <entry>\(90\)</entry>
                  <entry>\(8\)</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>\(4\)</entry>
                  <entry>\(160\)</entry>
                  <entry>\(16\)</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>\(8\)</entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>\(10\)</entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>\(12\)</entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                  <entry> </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>
          <para id="para-00004">Complete the statement.</para>
          <para id="para-00005">When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> increases by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>:</para>
          <para id="para-00006">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00007">Grows by increasing amounts but by decreasing growth factors.</para>
          <para id="para-00008">Changes exponentially. It doubles.</para>
          <para id="para-00009">Grows by decreasing amounts but by increasing growth factors.</para>
          <para id="para-00010">Changes logarithmically. It has decreased by one-half.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00011">Correct! When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> increases by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> grows by increasing amounts but by decreasing growth factors.</para>
          <para id="para-00012">Try again. Revisit activity 7.4.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00013">The correct answer is: When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> increases by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> grows by increasing amounts but by decreasing growth factors.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_8faaff31-6900-41de-8a2d-b80d6410eef6" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00014">When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> increases by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>:</para>
          <para id="para-00015">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00016">Grows by increasing amounts but by decreasing growth factors.</para>
          <para id="para-00017">Changes exponentially. It doubles.</para>
          <para id="para-00018">Grows by decreasing amounts but by increasing growth factors.</para>
          <para id="para-00019">Changes logarithmically. It has decreased by one-half.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00020">Correct! When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> increases by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> changes exponentially. It doubles.</para>
          <para id="para-00021">Try again. Revisit activity 7.4.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00022">The correct answer is: When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> increases by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> changes exponentially. It doubles.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_8e5a4f31-c589-4967-9720-c254217f286b" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00023">Will the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> be greater than or less than <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00024">Correct! The value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> will be greater than <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00025">Try again. Revisit activities 7.4.2 and 7.4.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00026">The correct answer is: The value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> will be greater than <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_5f718188-4505-4e71-963d-58f11b82edeb" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00027">Will the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> be greater than or less than <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00028">Correct! The value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> will be greater than <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00029">Try again. Revisit activities 7.4.2 and 7.4.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00030">The correct answer is: The value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> will be greater than <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="f994a359-6d8c-4c0e-a52a-1881e76fddee" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00031">Will the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> be greater than or less than <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00032">Correct! The value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> will be less than <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00033">Try again. Revisit activities 7.4.2 and 7.4.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00034">The correct answer is: The value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> will be less than <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="d5b7d872-1b85-4b80-b66c-70b4f87e9d07" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00035">Determine the following values of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00036">What is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00037">Correct! When <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>640</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00038">Try again. Revisit activity 7.4.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00039">The correct answer is: When <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>640</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_705515a5-0d88-4824-b33d-09be5291b64f" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00040">What is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00041">Correct! When <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>1000</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00042">Try again. Revisit activity 7.4.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00043">The correct answer is: When <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>1000</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="a4152af5-599e-42fa-9475-7c5b64709d38" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00044">What is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00045">Correct! When <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>1440</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00046">Try again. Revisit activity 7.4.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00047">The correct answer is: When <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>1440</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_37027873-e96f-4d70-8e77-f20e2bbd7858" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00048">Determine the following values of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00049">What is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00050">Correct! When <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>256</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00051">Try again. Revisit activity 7.4.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00052">The correct answer is: When <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>256</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="d5128dc7-5a90-47d9-833d-59629ceb89e7" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00010">
          <para id="para-00053">What is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00010">
          <para id="para-00054">Correct! When <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>1024</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00055">Try again. Revisit activity 7.4.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00056">The correct answer is: When <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>1024</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_7cea577a-7c41-4637-bb49-e502c9900882" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00011">
          <para id="para-00057">What is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00011">
          <para id="para-00058">Correct! When <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4096</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00059">Try again. Revisit activity 7.4.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00060">The correct answer is: When <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4096</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_5f1f6d4a-2063-423d-b50d-ef721491cfdc" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00012">
          <para id="para-00061">Choose the best statement that describes how the values of the exponential expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> and the quadratic expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> change as <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> becomes greater and greater.</para>
          <para id="para-00062">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00063">The value of the exponential expression grows much more quickly as <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> increases.</para>
          <para id="para-00064">The value of the quadratic expression grows much more quickly as <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> increases.</para>
          <para id="para-00065">They both grow at the same rate.</para>
          <para id="para-00066">There is no change in the values of the expressions when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> increases.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00012">
          <para id="para-00067">Correct! The value of the exponential expression grows much more quickly as <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> increases.</para>
          <para id="para-00068">Try again. Revisit activities 7.4.2 and 7.4.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00069">The correct answer is: The value of the exponential expression grows much more quickly as <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> increases.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_1ade4671-a4e8-4dfc-8bd1-b829a50b4e25" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00013">
          <para id="para-00070">Answer the following questions about functions <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00071">What type of expression is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>1.5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00013">
          <para id="para-00072">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>1.5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is an exponential expression.</para>
          <para id="para-00073">Try again. Revisit activities 7.4.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00074">The correct answer is: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>1.5</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is an exponential expression.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_7e9ff011-14bb-48df-a9e1-c15379946ea4" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00014">
          <para id="para-00075">What type of expression is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>500</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>345</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00014">
          <para id="para-00076">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>500</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>345</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is a quadratic expression.</para>
          <para id="para-00077">Try again. Revisit activities 7.4.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00078">The correct answer is: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>500</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>345</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is a quadratic expression.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_3161a9b3-dd78-407a-ba76-a63b3e7e778e" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00015">
          <para id="para-00079">The values of which function will eventually be greater for larger and larger values of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          <para id="para-00080">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00081">Function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00082">Function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00015">
          <para id="para-00083">Correct! The exponential function, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, will eventually be greater for larger and larger values of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00084">Try again. Revisit activities 7.4.2 and 7.4.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00085">The correct answer is: The exponential function, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, will eventually be greater for larger and larger values of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="f710b5e0-1775-4c25-8da8-e04c35ea4aff" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00016">
          <para id="para-00086">The table shows the values of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> for some values of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <table class="os-raise-skinnytable" id="table-00002">
            <tgroup cols="3">
              <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis></entry>
                  <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis></entry>
                  <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis></entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>\(1\)</entry>
                  <entry>\(4\)</entry>
                  <entry>\(100\)</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>\(2\)</entry>
                  <entry>\(16\)</entry>
                  <entry>\(400\)</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>\(3\)</entry>
                  <entry>\(64\)</entry>
                  <entry>\(900\)</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>\(4\)</entry>
                  <entry>\(256\)</entry>
                  <entry>\(1,600\)</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>\(5\)</entry>
                  <entry>\(1,024\)</entry>
                  <entry>\(2,500\)</entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>
          <para id="para-00087">Looking at the patterns in the table, choose the best answer to explain why, as the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> increases, the values of the exponential expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> will eventually overtake the values of the quadratic expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00088">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00089">The value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> grows by different factors and the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> grows by a factor of 4 every time.</para>
          <para id="para-00090">The value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> grows by a factor of 4 every time and the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> grows by different factors.</para>
          <para id="para-00091">The value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> grows by different factors and the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> grows by a factor of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> every time.</para>
          <para id="para-00092">The value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> grows by a factor of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> every time and the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> grows by different factors.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00016">
          <para id="para-00093">Correct! The value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> grows by different factors, and the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> grows by a factor of 4 every time.</para>
          <para id="para-00094">Try again. Revisit activities 7.4.4.</para>
          <para id="para-00095">The correct answer is: The value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>100</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> grows by different factors, and the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> grows by a factor of 4 every time.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
